  "pull_request": {
    "number": 243,
    "title": "feat(#120): add --max-warnings threshold",
    "body": "## Description\n\nAdds a \\--max-warnings N\\ flag to \\cargo-cost-lint\\ that exits non-zero when the total lint findings exceed the specified threshold. Also supports setting the threshold in \\\budget.toml\\ so CI and local runs agree.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nPreviously the linter was either advisory (warn) or blocking (deny), with nothing in between. Teams wanting CI enforcement on existing contracts with pre-existing findings couldn't turn on deny without breaking the build. A warning ceiling lets teams hold the line where they are and drive it down over time.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- \\--max-warnings N\\ CLI argument via clap\n- \\max_warnings\\ field in \\BudgetConfig\\ for \\\budget.toml\\ support (CLI takes precedence)\n- Warning counter tallies all findings (regardless of level)\n- On threshold exceed: prints \\error: number of warnings (N) exceeds --max-warnings (M)\\ and exits 1\n- Without the flag, exit behavior is unchanged\n- \\--max-warnings 0\\ is documented as strict mode\n\n## Usage\n\n`\bash\n# Fail if any warnings exist (strict mode)\ncargo cost-lint --max-warnings 0\n\n# Allow up to 5 warnings, fail at 6+\ncargo cost-lint --max-warnings 5\n`\n\nOr in \\\budget.toml\\:\n`\toml\n[budget]\nmax_warnings = 0\n`\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Action |\n|------|--------|\n| \\cargo-cost-lint/src/main.rs\\ | Added \\--max-warnings\\ CLI arg, \\BudgetConfig.max_warnings\\, warning counting logic, threshold check |\n| \\README.md\\ | Documented the flag with ratchet workflow examples |\n\nCloses #120",
